msm-vidc: keep V4L2_FL_USES_V4L2_FH (6.18 v4l2_open() rejects opens without it)

What: drop the 5.4 clear_bit(V4L2_FL_USES_V4L2_FH, &vdev->flags) from msm_v4l2_open().
Applies after 0024 (same hunk area as its v4l2_fh_add(fh, filp)).

Why / evidence:
- 6.18 ack/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-dev.c:437-441 (v4l2_open): after fops->open()
  succeeds, `if (WARN_ON(!test_bit(V4L2_FL_USES_V4L2_FH, &vdev->flags)))` calls
  fops->release() and returns -ENODEV. "All drivers must use v4l2_fh." 6.12 has no such check.
- msm_v4l2_vidc.c:257 cleared the (per-vdev) flag right after msm_vidc_open() ->
  setup_event_queue() -> v4l2_fh_init() set it, so on 6.18 every open of the decoder and
  encoder nodes would WARN, tear the instance down again and fail: no HW codec at all.
- The clear only mattered on 6.12, where the core looked at the flag to decide whether
  file->private_data is a v4l2_fh (6.12 v4l2-ioctl.c:2289ff, 3071). 6.18 ignores the flag
  there: file_to_v4l2_fh() (include/media/v4l2-fh.h:68) is used unconditionally in
  v4l2-ioctl.c:2298-2458, 3071. So keeping the flag changes nothing else on 6.18:
  vfh->ctrl_handler = vdev->ctrl_handler = NULL (vidc never sets vdev/v4l2_dev ctrl_handler;
  its handler is inst->ctrl_handler), so control ioctls still reach the ext-ctrl ops of 0024;
  priority checks (INFO_FL_PRIO) run against the fh's V4L2_PRIORITY_DEFAULT from
  v4l2_fh_add() -> v4l2_prio_open(), which passes unless someone takes RECORD priority.

--- a/drivers612/gpu-video/video/msm/vidc/msm_v4l2_vidc.c
+++ b/drivers612/gpu-video/video/msm/vidc/msm_v4l2_vidc.c
@@ -254,7 +254,12 @@
 		}
 	}
 #endif
-	clear_bit(V4L2_FL_USES_V4L2_FH, &vdev->flags);
+	/*
+	 * bsp618/port: the 5.4 driver cleared V4L2_FL_USES_V4L2_FH here so that the 6.12 core
+	 * ignored its fh (no priority checks, own control ops). 6.18 v4l2_open() rejects an open
+	 * without the flag (WARN, ->release(), -ENODEV) and takes file->private_data as the fh
+	 * whatever the flag says, so the flag stays as v4l2_fh_init() set it.
+	 */
 	/* bsp618/port: 6.18 v4l2_fh_add(fh, filp) also sets filp->private_data = fh */
 	v4l2_fh_add(&vidc_inst->event_handler, filp);
 	trace_msm_v4l2_vidc_open_end("msm v4l2_open end");
